module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularImmersionPureCodimension
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Pullbacks
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.RegularImmersion
import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth

/-!
# The smooth diagonal with the chapter's pure-codimension convention

Source: blueprint main-20261015, sec-smooth-purity/sk-lem-diag-reg,
lem-pur-diagonal-regular-immersion, and sk-def-purity-conv
(blueprint: lem-pur-diagonal-regular-immersion).

The chapter's definition concerns positive codimension and separated finite-type schemes
over a field. Unlike the upstream affine-local predicate, it records stalk dimensions as
well as regular generators. The current blueprint_update removes the old tangent-bundle
conclusion. The rank-zero clopen case used by the consumer is expressed there directly.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The diagonal of a separated smooth map of pure positive relative dimension is regular
of that pure codimension, in the chapter's fixed separated finite-type field setting.
Source: main-20261015, sk-lem-diag-reg, lem-pur-diagonal-regular-immersion; the definition
of positive pure codimension in sk-def-purity-conv
(blueprint: lem-pur-diagonal-regular-immersion).

Proof: take etale standard-smooth charts of f using sbc-thm-etale-local-normal-form.
On the affine-space model the diagonal ideal is generated by the differences of the d
coordinates, a regular sequence of length d. Etale restriction and faithfully flat descent
identify these generators with the stalk kernel of the actual diagonal at each source
point; this is the regularity argument in isRegularImmersion_diagonal. Smoothness of p_1
and its section Delta identify the residue fields and give the local dimension equality
at the diagonal: dim O_W,Delta(x) = dim O_X,x + d. The affine Noetherian regular-sequence
quotient dimension formula gives the same equality. Thus both clauses of the recorded
IsRegularImmersionOfPureCodimension hold at every x. Positive d is precisely the chapter's
convention, not a new assumption on the consumer's rank-zero etale morphism. -/
theorem diagonal_isRegularImmersionOfPureCodimension
    (k : Type u) [Field k] {X Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (aY : Y ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k))
    [IsSeparated aY] [LocallyOfFiniteType aY] [QuasiCompact aY]
    (f : X ⟶ Y) [IsSeparated f] [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (d : ℕ) (hd : 1 ≤ d) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension d f] :
    IsRegularImmersionOfPureCodimension
      (pullback.fst f f ≫ f ≫ aY) (pullback.diagonal f) d := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
